  "note": "Borough elections, 15 January 1931, held under the revised system of an annual quota. Four members were returned for each ward from a single poll, one of whom the council afterwards recognised as the ward's alderman. John Cathy was the ward's alderman; the councillors in order of priority were Abraham, Millar and Capt. A. Crawford Browne."
